read_commands — resource-read tool mirror (DECIDED, planned)
============================================================

status: planned (2026-07-15)
spec: "resource-read tool mirrors" under "mcp resources".
umbrella: plans/resource_tool_mirrors.

what it is: a builtin tool alias for the
isabelle://theory/{name}/commands resource — the navigation map
(Ir.source_map: index, keyword, line, offset, file per command), how an
agent picks attach points for repl_init_from_source.

advertised metadata (sketch)
----------------------------

name          read_commands
description   "List a theory's Isar commands as a navigation map —
              index, keyword, line, offset, file per command — the
              attach points for repl_init_from_source. `start`/`count`
              window the list. Same content as the
              isabelle://theory/{name}/commands resource."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "theory": {"type": "string"},
                 "start":  {"type": "integer"},
                 "count":  {"type": "integer"}},
               "required": ["theory"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}

backing: zero new mechanism — the same resolution path
isabelle://theory/{name}/commands uses (image_theory normalization ->
tier -> Ir.source_map via MCP.ir; ?start=&count= windowing). filesystem
tier inherits whatever the resource answers (the open /commands spike in
plans/session_structure applies identically — the mirror does not
resolve it, it shares it). one function, two surfaces.

tests (sketch): [scala unit] row + dispatch + parity with the resource
read on Fake_Backend; [e2e] read commands by tool and by resource,
byte-identical payloads.
